127
00:09:01,841 --> 00:09:04,959
And a model for the deliverables:
the check sees Git state.

128
00:09:04,999 --> 00:09:09,454
It can't see whether you understood what
you did. Everything you hand in is what the

129
00:09:09,494 --> 00:09:10,471
check can't verify.

130
00:09:12,311 --> 00:09:17,169
First the sandbox. server.git is the
server, the part GitHub plays in real life.

131
00:09:17,209 --> 00:09:22,127
pr is the script that plays the pull-request
side. you is your clone, beside your

132
00:09:22,167 --> 00:09:25,311
teammates' clones, each with
its own name and email.

133
00:09:25,351 --> 00:09:30,208
evidence holds the files a stage writes
for you, and home holds the isolated Git

134
00:09:30,248 --> 00:09:31,065
configuration.

135
00:09:31,405 --> 00:09:34,869
Then the eight stages, as a
calendar of eight working days.

136
00:09:34,909 --> 00:09:39,738
Under the calendar, the loop of one stage.
The fourth step is the one people skip.

137
00:09:39,778 --> 00:09:44,132
The next stage's injection refuses to
run until the previous check passes.

138
00:09:44,172 --> 00:09:47,279
Nothing refuses to run when
your write-up is missing.

139
00:09:47,319 --> 00:09:48,883
That's your own discipline.

140
00:09:50,723 --> 00:09:54,536
The README has nine rules, and
they're the course in nine lines.

141
00:09:54,576 --> 00:09:57,607
Evidence before action.
Preserve before you change.

142
00:09:57,647 --> 00:10:01,581
The lowest-risk fix. main is never
rewritten, and never pushed to.

143
00:10:01,621 --> 00:10:06,217
A forced push names what it expects.
Verify with the commands that showed the

144
00:10:06,257 --> 00:10:09,649
problem. Say what you did not
verify. No names in causes.

145
00:10:09,689 --> 00:10:14,706
And the solutions stay closed until your
own deliverables for the stage are written.

146
00:10:15,046 --> 00:10:18,384
How to run it. All commands
are typed in the course root.

147
00:10:21,724 --> 00:10:27,094
Then for each stage: read the stage's
BRIEFING.md and nothing else in the stage

148
00:10:27,134 --> 00:10:31,135
directory. Work in the sandbox
with your evidence log open.

149
00:10:31,175 --> 00:10:35,724
Run the stage's check from the
course root. Write the deliverables.

150
00:10:35,764 --> 00:10:41,340
Apply the next stage with its inject.sh.
If a repair goes wrong, capstone/setup.sh

151
