00:15:14,863 --> 00:15:19,582
stage-01.md and its seven headings. Write
the symptom in one sentence without

211
00:15:19,622 --> 00:15:24,711
interpretation. Write three hypotheses,
each with a prediction and the command that

212
00:15:24,751 --> 00:15:29,470
separates it. Predict which claims in
the briefing will turn out to be wrong.

213
00:15:29,510 --> 00:15:30,150
Then begin.

214
00:15:30,490 --> 00:15:34,328
The challenge is the capstone
itself: all eight stages,

215
00:15:34,368 --> 00:15:40,110
capstone/stage-01-bug-in-production to
capstone/stage-08-hotfix-and-backport, each

216
00:15:40,150 --> 00:15:43,918
with its seven deliverables,
and the final postmortem.

217
00:15:43,958 --> 00:15:46,879
Plan about ten to fourteen hours in total.

218
00:15:48,719 --> 00:15:51,420
Read the question, then answer
out loud, in two minutes.

219
00:15:56,260 --> 00:16:00,983
The question asks for three things per
failure: the failure, how it's noticed, the

220
00:16:01,023 --> 00:16:05,339
guard. A strong answer gives several
failures of different kinds: one about

221
00:16:05,379 --> 00:16:10,160
evidence, one about choosing the old value,
one about the restoring push, one about

222
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:13,645
other people's clones, one about
what is claimed afterwards.

223
00:16:13,985 --> 00:16:18,487
For each, the sign by which you would notice
it, which is often something missing,

224
00:16:18,527 --> 00:16:21,477
and a guard that is a habit
or a command you can name.

225
00:16:21,517 --> 00:16:24,634
It ties the list to the ladder
of fixes and to the lease.

226
00:16:24,674 --> 00:16:27,791
You'll be living this question
for the next eight stages.

227
00:16:29,631 --> 00:16:30,558
Let's land this.

228
00:16:30,898 --> 00:16:35,473
The capstone is eight cumulative stages
in one sandbox at a fictional company;

229
00:16:35,513 --> 00:16:38,904
nobody names the cause, and
states of earlier days remain.

230
00:16:39,244 --> 00:16:44,604
Every stage delivers seven items: evidence
log, root cause, recovery, verification,

231
00:16:44,644 --> 00:16:49,483
prevention, a message to the team, a
message to the CTO; and at the end one

232
00:16:49,523 --> 00:16:50,849
blameless postmortem.

233
00:16:51,189 --> 00:16:55,407
The work is judged on seven dimensions
at four levels, and the outcome is

234
00:16:55,447 --> 00:16:58,265
"demonstrates senior-level
mastery" or "not yet".

235
00:16:58,605 --> 00:17:03,613
Seven findings disqualify, among them
rewriting main, a bare forced push, any Git

236
00:17:03,653 --> 00:17:08,847
action before revocation in the secret stage,
and reporting as verified what was not

237
00:17:08,887 --> 00:17:09,345
checked.

238
00:17:09,685 --> 00:17:14,260
Pull requests are played locally by the
pr script and two refs per pull request;

239
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:18,183
where you use power over the server,
you name the GitHub equivalent.

240
00:17:20,023 --> 00:17:25,018
Work one stage per sitting. Hand in each
stage's deliverables, to a reviewer or to

241
00:17:25,058 --> 00:17:29,317
your own notes directory with a date,
before you apply the next stage.

242
00:17:29,357 --> 00:17:34,045
Keep the walkthrough, the inject scripts
and the scripts under labs/capstone/

243
00:17:34,085 --> 00:17:34,475
closed.

244
00:17:34,815 --> 00:17:37,768
You've met the company, the
rules and the standard.

245
00:17:37,808 --> 00:17:42,581
Everything else you need is already yours.
The next video is the capstone debrief,

246
00:17:42,621 --> 00:17:47,395
reading your own work against the evaluation.
Please watch it only after all eight

247
00:17:47,435 --> 00:17:51,738
stages are handed in. Until then, look
at the state first and type second.

248
00:17:51,778 --> 00:17:53,147
See you in the next one.
